  "editorial": [
    "The right hand returns to E above an A-minor accompaniment at bars 23–24. This is distinct from bars 7–8.",
    "The first ending repeat returns to the printed 1. The 30 common bars are played twice, using the first ending on pass one and the second ending on pass two.",
    "Both numbered endings have identical notes. The second adds Fine and a fermata, held here for its nominal printed duration.",
    "Velocity 46 and 112 represent the shared pp and ff marks. Quarter = 132 is an editorial rehearsal tempo.",
    "The Larghetto, Tempo di Valse introduction, second strain, printed D.C. from the second strain and Waltz No. 2 are outside this excerpt."
